      "body": "## Background\n\nThe scheduler's non-overlap speculative path always passes `pp_proxy_tensors` to the spec worker (`srt/managers/scheduler.py` lines 4514 and 4527), but several spec-v2 workers have diverged on this signature.\n\nAudit of `python/sglang/srt/speculative/` on main:\n\n| Worker | `pp_proxy_tensors` |\n|---|---|\n| eagle_worker_v2.py | ✅ |\n| dflash_worker_v2.py | ✅ |\n| ngram_worker.py | ✅ |\n| dspark_worker_v2.py | ✅ |\n| multi_layer_eagle_worker_v2.py | ✅ |\n| frozen_kv_mtp_worker_v2.py | ❌ (this PR) |\n| uno_worker_v2.py | ❌ (this PR) |\n\n## Problem\n\nAny model served through FrozenKVMTPWorkerV2 or UnoWorkerV2 dies on the first scheduler step with:\n\n```\nTypeError: <Worker>.forward_batch_generation() got an unexpected keyword argument 'pp_proxy_tensors'\n```\n\n## Solution\n\nAdd `pp_proxy_tensors=None` (and forward it to target_worker) to both workers. The parameter is optional so all existing callers remain unaffected. This makes the interface consistent across all spec-v2 workers.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Python syntax verified with ast.parse on both edited files.\n- Signature change is purely additive (`pp_proxy_tensors=None`).\n\nResolves #40155\n\nSigned-off-by: yancy <yancy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38557273513](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38557273513)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38557273505](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38557273505)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38557273471](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38557273471)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
